<title>LATVIA: LUKOIL NOT TO BUILD LUBRICANTS PLANT - REPORT.</title>
<headline>LUKOIL NOT TO BUILD LUBRICANTS PLANT - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic subsidiary of Russian oil giant Lukoil will not build a car lubricants plant in Latvia but in Finland, newspaper Bizness i Baltiya said on Friday.</p>
<p>It quoted the manager of Lukoil Baltija Khaim Kogan as saying that Lukoil management made the decision but gave no reason for the change.</p>
<p>Lukoil Baltija last year bought an oil storage facility in the town of Olaine and said that it had plans to build a plant to make car lubcricants there.</p>
<p>-- Martinsh Gravitis, Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
